    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 142\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 6075, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the social services law, in relation to determi-\n      nation and  approval  of  reimbursement  rates  for  managed  care\n      providers under medicaid\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  legislation  would  create  additional  requirements  around the\nDepartment of Health's (DOH) development of actuarially sound  rates  of\npayment to Medicaid managed care plans, which currently are submitted by\nDOH's independent actuary to the federal government.\n \n  The  additional  steps and delays imposed by this bill could delay the\nability of DOH to submit its rate certifications to the federal  Centers\nfor  Medicare  & Medicaid Services (CMS) in a timely manner. CMS has the\nability to defer, delay or disallow the federal share of any  capitation\npayments  associated  with  untimely  rate  submissions. This bill would\nlikely lead to delays which could lead to billions of dollars in  finan-\ncial liabilities for New York's Medicaid program.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 142,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2023
